    # 7. TTS -- text to speech, for /audio/speech. Not ranked by a leaderboard and with no contract: no
    # ranking of speech models is read here, so the order is decided by hand. The fuller model comes
    # first and the lite one second, which is a model of its own and so, if Google counts the quota per
    # model (not checked), one that answers when the first is refused for quota. A text model never
    # belongs here and a speech model never belongs in a text cascade: "check_compose_template.py" holds
    # both, through "model_info.mode". Mistral's Voxtral is served but not routed to, for the reason given
    # above its commented entry. LiteLLM's own source, read 2026-11-22, applies "fallbacks" and
    # "model_group_alias" to /audio/speech as it does to chat, and a "response_format" other than "wav"
    # and "pcm", which Gemini cannot produce, is refused before any request leaves, so by both members alike.
{% if head['tts'] %}
    - tts: &tts_cascade
        - gemini-3-8-flash-tts
        - gemini-3-8-flash-lite-tts
{% for alias in aliases_of['tts'] %}
